Market Challenges
Soil composition, rainfall, drainage, and local geological conditions can vary significantly between project sites. These variations make it difficult to distinguish weathering-related carbon removal from natural background processes.

Service providers must also coordinate field teams, laboratories, project developers, and verification organisations. Establishing consistent sampling procedures and reliable data records across multiple locations remains a technical and operational challenge.

Market Restraints
Sampling expenses and uncertainty in field measurements can affect project economics. Developers may delay or reduce monitoring programmes when the cost of collecting and analysing samples is difficult to justify against expected carbon-removal outcomes.

Limited availability of qualified personnel and restricted site access can further constrain service delivery. Integration delays and pricing pressure may also influence procurement decisions, particularly for smaller projects.

